+## Customer-Facing Product Matrix SOP
+
+Before any release that touches onboarding, pricing, gating, upsells, permissions, or customer-facing docs, do a matrix audit from first principles.
+
+Hard rule:
+- Do not trust memory, old marketing copy, or an enum name alone. Build the Basic/Pro matrix from the actual app behavior.
+
+Required review surfaces:
+- feature enums / license gates
+- runtime handlers
+- settings rows
+- shortcuts
+- menu labels
+- context menus
+- onboarding lists
+- upsell windows
+- README / website pricing tables / comparison tables
+
+Required decisions:
+- Pro must not leak through free paths.
+- Table-stakes features must not be unnecessarily Pro-gated.
+- If a feature is premium, the user should learn that before or at the interaction point, not only after an error.
+- If marketing says Basic includes a feature, Basic mode must truly support it.
+- Use `Basic includes...` / `Pro includes...` framing instead of awkward internal or blunt `paid` wording.
+- Keep the matrix and tone consistent across apps that share SaneUI onboarding unless a documented product exception exists.
+
+Required proof:
+- at least one source test or deterministic assertion for any matrix change that is easy to regress
+- at least one Mini visual artifact when the change is user-facing
+
+## Permission UX SOP
+
+For permission-related work, treat onboarding and runtime recovery as one customer experience.
+
+Required checks before release:
+1. The onboarding permission buttons use the real request-first API when macOS supports it.
+2. Opening System Settings is the fallback, not the only path, unless the OS truly requires that.
+3. The permissions are ordered for the real user journey, not arbitrarily.
+4. Copy explains restart/relaunch requirements only on the permissions that actually need them.
+5. The same permission can be recovered later from the runtime feature path if the user skipped it during onboarding.
+6. The permissions screen fits all required grant actions on one screen without scroll.
+7. Any permission that forces restart/relaunch is last unless there is a documented reason otherwise.
+8. If setup is interrupted by restart/relaunch, the app should restore or resume the onboarding flow when feasible.
+
+`ruby scripts/validation_report.rb` reads the newest available status snapshot and blocks false `READY TO SHIP` results.
 
